<title>JAPAN: Sakakibara says no comment on current dlr/yen rate.</title>
<headline>Sakakibara says no comment on current dlr/yen rate.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senior Finanance Ministry official Eisuke Sakakibara said on Tuesday he would not comment on the current dollar/yen rate.</p>
<p>Asked about the dollar's dip below 113 yen earlier in the afternoon, Sakakibara, head of the ministry's International Finance Bureau, told Reuters: &quot;I'm not going to comment on currencies.&quot;</p>
<p>The dollar dipped below 113 yen in late Tokyo trade after falling nearly three full yen from its New York close.</p>
</text>
